reate and create and  we don't give them that space in school  in school they're sitting down learning  from a curriculum so I'm really  interesting in in creating that space  and and you know before kovat happened  like I was already thinking about doing  it in the online space just so that kids  from different countries could just join  and then it's a space for kids to create  different things they come in with a  problem that they want to solve and I  help them and I provide them with the  resources so that they  worked it through and come up with a  prototype and solve a problem that  they're interested in a real problem and  I feel like I've seen how through that  process they're learning so many you  know so many things they're learning how  to do research how we like talk about  their ideas how to incorporate feedback  and change things and to me that is the  kind of learning that is gonna be more  valuable for kids in the future right  forget about what's going on in school  we've already talked about how that's  like they're not preparing kids for the  future but if we open more centers or  you know creative studios or like I'm  doing online spaces for kids to just go  in and execute their ideas and try them  out two things are gonna happen one we I  do feel like we're gonna have more kids  that are fifteen sixteen like with their  own company so with their own products  out there because they're gonna have  tried so many times and I don't have you  seen a kid when they're into something  they won't stop until they get to what  they want to so it's a matter of  providing them to space and the  resources to create and create and  create and create and and that's kind of  like a makerspace  right for kids so that's kind of what  I'm envisioning that kids think more  nowadays and hopefully more people start  doing things like this so one of the  things I've always been fascinated by is  I think a disproportionate amount of  CEOs and founders of very large tec